=============================================
UBUNTU STALE SESSION MANAGER - README
=============================================

DESCRIPTION:
This tool provides system administrators with a robust solution for managing stale user sessions on Ubuntu servers. It features both interactive menu-driven operation and command-line options for automation.

KEY FEATURES:
- Interactive terminal menu system
- Configurable idle time threshold
- User whitelist protection
- Multiple termination methods (SIGTERM/SIGKILL)
- Email notification capability
- Dry-run mode for testing
- Comprehensive logging
- Easy installation/uninstallation
- Systemd service integration

INSTALLATION METHODS:

1. ONE-LINE WEB INSTALL (RECOMMENDED):
   curl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/[your-account]/ubuntu-stale-session-manager/main/install.sh | sudo bash

2. MANUAL INSTALLATION:
   wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/[your-account]/ubuntu-stale-session-manager/main/install.sh
   chmod +x install.sh
   sudo ./install.sh

3. UNINSTALLATION:
   sudo /usr/local/bin/stale-session-manager --uninstall
   OR
   sudo ./install.sh --uninstall

DEPENDENCIES:
- mailutils (for email notifications)
- curl or wget (for web installation)
- Standard Ubuntu server utilities

CONFIGURATION:
The script automatically creates a config file at:
/etc/stale_session_manager.conf

You can edit this file directly or use the built-in configuration menu.

AUTOMATED CLEANING:
The installer creates a systemd service for scheduled cleaning.

To enable daily at 3 AM:
sudo systemctl enable stale-session-cleaner.timer

Service configuration:
/etc/systemd/system/stale-session-cleaner.service

USAGE:
Interactive Mode:
  sudo stale-session-manager

Command Line Options:
  --dry-run    Simulation mode (no actual termination)
  --force      Use SIGKILL if SIGTERM fails
  --idle N     Set idle threshold in minutes
  --notify     Enable email notifications
  --email      Set admin email address
  --whitelist  Set protected users (comma separated)
  -h, --help   Show help message

CRON ALTERNATIVE:
To run daily at 3 AM with 60 minute idle threshold:
0 3 * * * /usr/local/bin/stale-session-manager --idle 60 --notify

LOGGING:
All activities are logged to:
/var/log/stale_session_manager.log

FILES INSTALLED:
- /usr/local/bin/stale-session-manager (main script)
- /etc/stale_session_manager.conf (configuration)
- /var/log/stale_session_manager.log (log file)
- /etc/systemd/system/stale-session-cleaner.service (service file)

SECURITY NOTES:
1. Always verify scripts from external sources
2. The web installation uses HTTPS for security
3. Consider reviewing the script before pipe-to-bash installation

